  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nOutreach Talks\nOxfordshire's Military Heritage in 50 Objects\n\nThe Oxfordshire Yeomanry D Squadron 'pub' sign.\n\nThe museum holds a fascinating collection of over 14,500 objects. Fifty objects across the archive have been selected to provide moments of insight into the county’s military history. These objects reflect on the personal stories of not only those who fought in both The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry and Oxfordshire Yeomanry regiments, but also those living in Oxfordshire who have been impacted by conflict.\n\nCombine a talk or archive tour with a visit to the museum, or we can come to you! Use the contact form below to enquire about booking a talk for your group, club or society.\n\nTalks start at £65 (plus travel costs for outreach talks). There are 5 different variations of the talk focusing on 5 themed sets of the 50 Objects, following themes such as Leading the Charge: Oxfordshire Regiments Making History; Sending A Message - The Evolution of Military Communications; Solace and Salvation: How simple objects comforted those who served; Home Fires: Life on the Oxfordshire Home Front; Identity: Shared identity, belonging and fighting spirit.\n\nBook two talks for £115 (plus travel costs for outreach talks).\n\nDownload a PDF outline of our Outreach Talks and Tours >>\n\nGet a preview of our favourite 50 Objects here!\n\nBOOK A 50 OBJECTS TALK\nYour Name\nYour Email\nYour Phone Number\nOrganisation Name\nOrganisation Address\nIs this the same location that the talk will take place?\nYes\nNo\nWill the talk be in person or online?\nIn person\nOnline\nPreferred dates and times for the talk(s)\nCan you give an estimated number of attendees for the talk?\nWhether online or in person\nYour Message\nLet us know any other information, or if you have any other questions here\nContact Us\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
